---
type: statement
kind: definition
---

A _topological manifold of dimension $\dim$_ or a _topological $\dim$-manifold_ is a topological space $\manifold$ with the following properties.

- $\manifold$ is Hausdorff (points may be separated by open sets).
- $\manifold$ is second-countable (countable basis for topology).
- $\manifold$ is locally Euclidean of dimension $\dim$ (each point of $\manifold$ has a neighborhood homeomorphic to an open subset of $\bbR^\dim$).

A _coordinate chart_ on $\manifold$ is a pair $(\open, \chart)$, where $\open \subseteq \manifold$ is open and $\chart: \open \rightarrow \hat\open$ is a homeomorphism with $\hat\open = \chart(\open) \subseteq \bbR^\dim$.
When $\point \in \manifold$ is such that $\chart(\point) = 0$, we say the chart $\chart$ is _centered at $\point$_.
